; A handler clause that does NOT call `resume` must DISCARD the continuation
; (algebraic-effects abort): the handle's result is the clause value 999, and
; the `[+ 1 ...]` around `[F.fail]` never runs. The EIR VM and the legacy
; interpreter now AGREE on 999 (enforced in backend_parity.rs CORPUS as
; effect-abort-discards-continuation).
; expect-fail: wasm — codegen compiles the handler tail-resumptively, so it
; still resumes with the clause value and computes 1 + 999 = 1000.
[effect F [fail [] Int]]
[fn body [] [+ 1 [F.fail]]]
[fn main []
  [println [handle [body] [F.fail] 999]]]
